# mv — caps.decl
#
# Wave: R50 (Wave 2)
# Doc:  design/tooling/r49-r50-plan.md §5.7 in the paideia-os repo.
#
# mv moves one path onto another. Every M1 invocation degenerates to
# a same-directory rename — src and dst share a parent, so the two
# write authorities collapse into ONE KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write, <parent>).
# M2 splits the two out again for the cross-directory case (rename
# opens ONE TXN that touches BOTH parents; the caps.decl still names
# them separately so exec-time cap_manifest_verify catches a caller
# that forgot to hand down one side or the other).
#
# The M1 baseline is:
#
#   * KIND_USER (self)             — identity root. mv checks the
#                                    caller's KIND_USER tail before it
#                                    touches an inode (D3 audit-first,
#                                    R48.M1 KIND_USER = 0x190 substrate
#                                    at paideia-os
#                                    src/kernel/core/cap/kind_user.pdx).
#
#   * KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)   — baseline pipe substrate (R20b,
#                                    base kind 5). Consumers use it
#                                    for stdout/stderr rendering. M3
#                                    wires libpdx-semantic-pipe on top
#                                    for MoveRecord[] emission.
#
#   * KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write, <src-parent>) — write authority on the
#                                    directory that holds src. M1 uses
#                                    it to unlink the source dirent
#                                    inside the TXN.
#                                    KIND_PDXFS_FILE = 0x195 (R42
#                                    substrate, landed in paideia-os
#                                    commit 411ad0e).
#
#   * KIND_PDXFS_FILE(write, <dst-parent>) — write authority on the
#                                    directory that will hold dst. M1
#                                    uses it to link the target dirent
#                                    inside the SAME TXN. For same-dir
#                                    rename src-parent == dst-parent
#                                    and the two caps refer to the
#                                    same underlying dir inode; the
#                                    caps.decl still names them
#                                    separately so M2's cross-dir path
#                                    is a code change, not a manifest
#                                    change.
#
#   * KIND_PDXFS_TXN (invoke, mint) — transaction authority so mv can
#                                    open one TXN, thread the unlink
#                                    + link through it, and commit
#                                    atomically. invoke is used for
#                                    query ops on an existing txn;
#                                    mint is what mv needs to open a
#                                    new one at invocation.
#                                    KIND_PDXFS_TXN = 0x196 (R42
#                                    substrate).
#
# --- elevate-broker binding (M3-004) -----------------------------------
# Cross-user-boundary destination requires an elevate hop: mv borrows
# KIND_USER(sign, dst_owner_key) from svc.elevate-broker for a 60s
# window so pdxfs_inode_rebind_owner can re-sign the moved inode
# under the destination-user's key. Best-effort HINT -- a refused
# elevate falls through to the M2-004 graceful-degrade path (inode
# keeps old owner tail; verbose diagnostic flags the degrade).
# KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL = 0x191 (R48.M7 substrate at paideia-os
# src/kernel/core/ipc/elevate_broker.pdx). Live at HEAD 2026-08-22.
#
# --- R90-XREPO.010 substrate adoption note (mv#28) ----------------------
# R90-XREPO.010 landed the REAL PdxFS v1 TXN syscalls this file's
# KIND_PDXFS_TXN row already anticipated: sys_pdxfs_txn_open (sysno
# 70), sys_pdxfs_txn_commit (104), sys_pdxfs_txn_abort (105),
# sys_pdxfs_stat_by_inode (106), sys_pdxfs_undo_write (107) --
# design/kernel/pdxfs-syscalls.md §3 in the paideia-os repo is the
# authoritative source; src/pdxfs_txn.pdx (mv#34) wires mv onto them.
# This DOES NOT change the requires: list below -- the R90 substrate
# still gates txn_open behind a KIND_PDXFS_TXN mint exactly as M2-001
# already declared (unlike cp's R90-XREPO.013.M3-003 landing, which
# added a NEW KIND_PDXFS_VOL row for its own outer-TXN re-wire (cp#31)
# -- cp's txn_open call passes a volume-scoping argument mv does not
# yet need at same-device/same-user scope). Reconciliation verified
# against cp/caps.decl's own R90-XREPO adoption note and cp/CHANGELOG.
# md's sysno cross-references as the sibling-tool precedent.
#
# sys_semantic_send caveat (v1.3.0, mv#31) -- mirrors cp's own note:
# the sysno-115 producer path (Pipe::pipe_emit_move_record, src/
# pipe.pdx) takes no cap slot at the R107-M0-001 landing. If a future
# R107 wave adds a per-schema KIND_SEMANTIC_PIPE gate for the send
# side, this file grows a new row at that time.
requires:
  - KIND_USER (self)
  - KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT (invoke)
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <src-parent>)
  - KIND_PDXFS_FILE (write, <dst-parent>)
  - KIND_PDXFS_TXN (invoke, mint)
  - KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL (invoke, svc.elevate-broker)

# Declared output schemas — the semantic-pipe schema records mv emits
# on the sys_semantic_send ring (v1.3.0, mv#31/mv#33 -- see src/
# pipe.pdx and src/move_schema.pdx). Superseded/additive to the older
# M3-001 fd-1 stub blob (Schema module, unchanged by this release).
declares_output_schemas:
  - MoveRecord@0.2 (schema=0xE0604D560002, len=120, via=sys_semantic_send)
